Z||000003||Songman||08-15-2001||08:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tabs:<BR><B>there were 3 real indys made!!!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>And I have all three of them at my house and you can't have one, Jim! hehe<P>Don't I wish!<P>Jim, someone posted a link last week to a place that sold performance parts. Whoever it was said they even listed SD parts. I went to the site and they even listed and SD block! I'd say do a search on the forum on something including Super Duty, unless the person that posted it sees this and lists it again.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||08-15-2001||08:53 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by beachbomb:<BR><B>Hey all, i have a couple questions!<BR>1)Does anyone know how many Indy fieros were actually at Indy pacing the indy race cars around the track?<P>2)Does anyone know if any of these Indy fieros still exsist, and if so, where?<P>3)Does anyone know where an SD4 engine is?any info is greatly appreciated, thanks..jim(2 '84 Indys)<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigzach_25.JPG">   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>1) There were 3 REAL Indy Pace Cars and 2 PPG pace cars built later.<P>2) The real Pace cars are in Indy, Chicago, and Pontiac, Michigan.<P>3) Used SD4's can be bought thru <BR>Vanderley Engineering <BR>316 libertyville Dr. <BR>Biloxi, MS 39531 <BR>(601) 435-1582 <BR> New from:<BR>Kansas Racing Products <BR>At present their website appears to be down.<BR>(Possilby attacked by one of the virus' ???)<P><BR> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Max The Chainsaw||08-15-2001||09:56 PM||||I could be wrong (Happens a lot.  LOL) but aren't 2 of them on display at the Indy 500 museum and the Chicago Science and Industry museum?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||LAMBO||08-16-2001||03:36 PM||||There was a post a couple of months ago that gave a phone number to someone in Cincy, Ohio that had two street SD4's for sale. One of them was a 245 hp and the other was a 280 hp. The 245 could be bought for around $5K. A lot cheaper than KRP's complete motors. He also had a full race motor, but don't know the specs on it. Try doing a search.<BR>Todd||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wild_86_Custom||08-16-2001||04:06 PM||||One pace car Pontiac Motors has it went to the Dust Off this year and the other two are in the Indy 500 museum.<BR>                  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||08-16-2001||08:44 PM||||Im not sure that Vanderley Engineering still exists, I had been trying to find out more about two GTP engines that they were selling. These were SD-4 DOHC! I think they may have gone away, either that or they have become very quiet online...||||reg||9
Z||000009||FieroKyle||08-16-2001||10:52 PM||||I think this is funny on what about I am gonna say but its probably cruel.....<P>Alright, imagine this in your head. Alright the second caution of the 1984 Indy 500 and the pace car comes off pit road. HEY LOOK! The pace car is engulfed in flames in turn two!!! The back end just rolling out with flames as everyone looks on. If that would of happened, I think the 85's would have been the last production year.||||reg||1
